<!-- QtUiPlus :: Bindings.xml

     Binding commands for the action pages this client has none of its own for.
     ACTIONBUTTON follows whichever page bar 1 shows and the four MULTIACTIONBAR
     commands cover slots 25 to 72 (bars 2-5), which leaves bar 6 (the main
     bar's page 2, slots 13 to 24) and the class/bonus pages 7 to 10 with no
     key of their own. Those are the last five bars, sorted after the bindable
     ones.
     Declaring them here puts them in the client's real binding table: SetBinding
     writes them, SaveBindings persists them, and they appear in the stock Key
     Bindings window under the QtUiPlus headers.

     This is the path UnrealPfUI uses on this same client for the identical case
     (its Bindings.xml declares PFPAGING and PFSTANCE commands whose bodies call
     pfActionButton). WORKING_SOURCE, not runtime verified.

     runOnUp matches that working source: the body runs on key release, so a held
     key cannot repeat the action.

     The client loads this file itself, which is why it is not listed in the
     .toc, and it loads it only at start-up: a new command needs a full client
     restart, not a /reload.

     The body is guarded because a binding can fire before the module that
     installs QtUiPlusActionButton has finished loading.

     Note for future edits: an XML comment may not contain a double hyphen. A
     malformed comment makes the client reject this entire file, and every bar
     below silently loses its keys. -->
<Bindings>
  <!-- Bar 6 (main bar page 2, slots 13-24) -->
  <Binding name="QTUIPLUSBAR6BUTTON1" runOnUp="true" header="QTUIPLUSBAR6">if QtUiPlusActionButton then QtUiPlusActionButton(6,1) end</Binding>
  <Binding name="QTUIPLUSBAR6BUTTON2" runOnUp="true">if QtUiPlusActionButton then QtUiPlusActionButton(6,2) end</Binding>
